<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-24">24 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Brooklyn Bridge opens across the East River</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After fourteen years of construction, the bridge linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> and Brooklyn opened. It was then the longest suspension bridge in the world, the first to use <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> wire cables.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vienna" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vienna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-5">5 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Express d'Orient makes its first run from Paris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Georges Nagelmackers's luxury train service left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. That October it was extended towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and as the Orient Express it became a legend of rail travel.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-26">26 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Krakatoa begins its cataclysmic eruption</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The volcano of Krakatoa in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda Strait</a> began its climactic eruption, culminating in explosions the next day heard thousands of kilometres away. Tsunamis killed more than 36,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda Strait</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-20">20 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Peru and Chile sign the Treaty of Ancón</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed at Ancón, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>, the treaty settled the two nations' remaining territorial differences as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>'s part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a> came to an end. By its terms Peru ceded the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarapaca">Tarapacá</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chile">Chile</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Republic of Chile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ancon">Treaty of Ancón</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarapaca">Tarapacá</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1883" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1883.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-hue-1883">Treaty of Huế (1883)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Huế of 25 August 1883, known as the Harmand Treaty after the French negotiator Jules Harmand, was imposed on the Nguyễn court after French forces stormed the forts guarding Huế.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shaykan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shaykan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shaykan">Battle of Shaykan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Shaykan was fought on 3–5 November 1883 in the forest of Shaykan near El Obeid in Kordofan, Sudan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/la-marsa-convention" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-marsa-convention.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/la-marsa-convention">La Marsa Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The La Marsa Convention was an agreement signed on 8 June 1883 between France and Ali III ibn al-Husayn, bey of Tunis.</p></div></li></ol></section>
